# Cloudflare's own header-injection convention (same file Netlify popularized;
# Cloudflare's static-asset serving reads it the same way as _redirects).
# Lives in public/ so Expo Router's static export copies it into dist/
# automatically, same reasoning as _redirects and .htaccess next to it.
#
# script-src has no 'unsafe-inline': that's the header actually doing
# something against XSS. style-src needs it — React Native Web renders
# every component's style as an inline `style` attribute, not a stylesheet
# class, so disallowing inline styles would break the entire app's
# rendering, not just tighten security.
#
# The lone sha256 hash in script-src is the Telegram Login Widget's own
# doing: telegram-login.tsx only ever injects a <script src=...> pointing
# at telegram.org (already covered by the host allowance), but the widget
# script that loads from there then injects one small literal inline
# <script> of its own to finish rendering the button/iframe. There's no
# way to add 'unsafe-inline' just for Telegram's script without opening it
# up for everyone else's too, so this pins the one exact script Telegram's
# widget is known to inject, by content hash, instead — the browser's own
# CSP violation error reports the required hash directly when it changes
# (Telegram has shipped the same one for a long time, but a future widget
# version could rotate it).
#
# img-src allows any https: origin rather than naming hosts one by one —
# book covers come from Google Books, Open Library, and user uploads to
# Supabase storage, and Google/Open Library's own cover CDNs are not fixed,
# stable hostnames worth pinning here.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://telegram.org 'sha256-67fhrP0+BkBqmgGGXTtgiVO/9EQs3QruYNU/7fnRkI8='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https: data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://www.googleapis.com https://openlibrary.org https://covers.openlibrary.org; frame-src https://telegram.org https://oauth.telegram.org; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
